id: ops-release-npm-runtime
title: Release and CI install Dependabot locks with the same pinned npm
description: Daily Release run 42412827958 failed before publishing because trusted tool and audit installs used npm 10.9.3 from Node 22.18.0 against the 091124b lock. Standardize release and CI on exact npm 11.21.0 before any locked install.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-11-07T23:40:56.448Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-07T23:46:05.602Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Inventory every workflow and script npm install with before and after runtimes; Pin and verify npm before trusted tool, provenance and caller installs while retaining node-version and ignore-scripts; PR CI executes the exact release production install against both committed locks; Document passing fixed and failing npm 10.9.3 runs against the unchanged 091124b fixture; Focused tests and typecheck pass; CI is the full gate; docs explain the caller runtime"
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T23:40:58.995Z",pi-agent,"Repro: on main 091124b (Dependabot #254), npm 10.9.3 ci --omit=dev --ignore-scripts --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund reports EUSAGE: glob@13.0.6 does not satisfy glob@13.0.7. Reported npm 11.17.0 succeeds. CI already selects 11.21.0; release selects 11.19.0 only after tool bootstrap, while audit/alert/recover/Bun hooks inherit bundled npm. Plan: pin packageManager to 11.21.0, install and verify it immediately after setup-node in all reusable jobs, add isolated exact-command root/private PR CI smoke checks, retain lock bytes and lifecycle suppression."
  "2026-11-07T23:44:59.543Z",pi-agent,"Revert proof: immutable 091124b package.json/package-lock.json fixtures on real Node 22.18.0: exact npm ci --omit=dev --ignore-scripts --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund exits 1 with npm 10.9.3 (EUSAGE; glob@13.0.6 does not satisfy glob@13.0.7), exits 0 with npm 11.21.0 (5 production packages). Private provenance fixture passes with both npm versions (52 packages). All four runs preserve the lock SHA-256. In a disposable source copy, retaining new tests/manifests but restoring only both workflows to 091124b gives 0/3 pass and 3 failures; restoring fixed workflows gives 3/3 pass, no skips. Original worktree is never reverted. npm 11.21.0 engine range ^20.17.0 || >=22.9.0 admits the Node 22.18.0 default."
  "2026-11-07T23:45:00.919Z",pi-agent,"Local gates: focused workflow/runtime tests 43/43 pass, zero failures/skips; npm run typecheck and npm run build:test pass; lint passes; duplication 0% (0/37768 lines, 141 sources, zero clones); docstring 48 files/370 declarations pass. Full npm/Bun release gates and Windows consumers are delegated to PR CI per task scope. docs/reusable-release.md contains the complete before/after install inventory. Both committed locks remain byte-identical to 091124b. No release dispatch, publication or merge performed."
  "2026-11-07T23:46:03.257Z",pi-agent,The new CI lock-smoke shell step also ran unchanged locally under pinned npm 11.21.0 against fresh copies of the current root and private manifests/locks; both installations succeeded. PM linked-test execution uses the default sandbox context; no test-run artifacts are written into the package tracker.
